some of you guys have been asking us to  make a video concerning the apple watch  series 6 that we should be expecting  this fall  and the reason we waited so long to make  this video is because there weren't  really any good leaks and rumors out  there  until now so in this video i'm going to  discuss the expected announcement date  the release date all of the leaks and  rumors we currently have  which features you should expect and  whether or not you should actually wait  for the series 6  instead of just buying a different apple  watch right now let's first try and  figure out when we should expect it to  get released  apple has already announced that the  2020 iphones will launch a few weeks  later than usual  now this is very vague because it could  be three weeks or it could be  five weeks but i think it would be a  mistake to wait too long  and this is very important because apple  always releases their new apple watch  updates  alongside their new iphones twitter  leaker comia  initially posted that the series 6 would  be available to order on september 8th  a wednesday which assumes that's the day  of the september event  and then it would ship on september 18th  which is  the following friday but a few days  later  he then said that the event might not  happen on the 8th  but he's sure that it won't be in  october  however john prosser another leaker  mentioned that he thinks the iphone 12  announcement will actually happen  in october so things seem a bit  uncertain at this moment  he seems to think that they'll go on  sale in mid-october  so this would mean that the event could  take place on october 6th  or the 7th with the shipping date of  october 16th  for the apple watch series 6. i  personally wouldn't expect it to be  any later than that because apple is  also rumored to be having a special  event  for their new apple silicon max and  that's dated for october 27th  so apple wouldn't want those events too  close to each other but there's also the  chance that apple will host the iphone  event sometime  in september and then simply delay the  ship dates  out into october so it's a bit of a toss  up right now  now getting into all the leaks we  currently have right now  there's rumored to be an air power mini  for 99  and the full version of air power for  249 dollars  which will be announced alongside the  apple watch series 6.  and john prosser has mentioned that  apple finally got  the apple watch to work with the air  power wireless charging mat  so that's definitely reassuring and  according to camilla  the airpower mini will be available  sooner with the large air power  shipping at the end of the year now  getting into apple watch specific leaks  some ios 14 code leaked in march  pointing to apple working on a new  blood oxygen monitoring feature this is  a very big deal because a lot of  businesses right now  are requiring people to wear a mask  and these obviously make it harder to  breathe or else they wouldn't be doing  anything  so essentially your apple watch series 6  will tell you when your blood oxygen  level is dropping  letting you know if you should go  outside take off your mask  and get some fresh air and by the way we  actually sell  high quality apple product pattern masks  that are made  in the usa they're very soft and  comfortable  and you can find them in our merch shelf  just below this video  in both black and in white very recently  digitimes reported that apple will add  this feature  to the apple watt series 6. they  mentioned that the new model will  feature  updated bio sensors that detect blood  oxygen  greatly improve sleep monitoring and it  will incorporate an  mems based accelerator and gyroscope  which should be much more accurate  for precise measurements for things like  working out and step monitoring  so as you guys know from apple's wwdc  event  apple is adding sleep tracking to watch  os 7. now my brother max tested the beta  version  and he said it's very limited and it  doesn't work very well right now  so it would make sense that the new  sensors in the series 6 apple watch  will greatly improve sleep tracking now  he also said that battery life was an  issue because it obviously requires your  watch to be on  at night so we should expect apple to  work on improving the battery life  for the series 6. just a couple of days  ago a 303.8 milliamp hour battery was  leaked  which should be destined for the new  apple watch  the current series 5 has a 296 milliamp  hour battery  so there definitely is an improvement  there now don't expect the apple watch  itself to get thicker  because apple did remove force touch in  the upcoming watchos 7 update so that  means they have more room  for a larger battery comedia also  tweeted showing that same battery size  as we saw in that leak  but he also included two other battery  sizes  presumably for the smaller 40 millimeter  size and a model with cellular  now as far as the performance an app  developer who has access to apple's  developer transition kit  for the switch to apple silicon found a  new code  that points to new apple chips including  an s6  chip for the apple watch and since we  know that apple's upcoming iphones  and apple silicon max are going to be  built using tsmc's new 5 nanometer  process  we can expect the s6 chip to be even  more efficient  leading to the same great performance  while getting better battery life  which will help with sleep tracking way  back in november of 2019  ming chakra stated that he believes the  apple watch series 6  will come with a new liquid crystal  polymer flexible circuit board that will  improve performance  water resistance and wireless  transmission which will help with both  wi-fi  and cellular speeds and in august of  2019  apple filed for a patent to enable their  apple watch to come with a new antenna  array  that would allow for a larger range of  cellular frequencies  basically pointing to apple working on a  5g apple watch  now since apple is releasing 5g iphones  this year  there's a chance that we could get a 5g  apple watch  but honestly i think it's a bit too  early because it's going to negatively  impact battery life  and 5g hasn't really seen wide  implementation yet  way back in july of 2019 some sources  claim that the new apple watch series 6  could come with a micro led display  however  leaker love to dream claim that the  series 6 will actually continue  using the same display as the series 5  so it's definitely a toss-up  but in my personal opinion since the  iphone 12 is getting a new square edge  design  and the apple silicon max are coming  later this year  it would make sense for apple to change  up the exterior look or design  a bit to entice users to upgrade since  the series 5  only had minimal changes now there was  somebody who found some new code in ios  14 beta  showing slimmer bezels compared to  before and the removal of the side  button  which could be switched to using a  static haptic button  instead of an actual protruding button  this change would also help with water  resistance  this could also match up to a rumor back  in march that apple is adding a touch id  fingerprint sensor  to the apple watch series 6 which would  work perfectly  in place of the current side button now  if apple did truly slim the bezels of  the display once again  that change alone with the new bio  sensors  might be enough for a lot of people to  upgrade so with all of those leaks and  rumors out of the way  let's talk about whether you should wait  for the series 6 or not well since we're  only a month or two away  i would definitely suggest waiting  unless you absolutely need a watch right  now  and you also have to ask yourself how  much does blood oxygen monitoring  and sleep tracking matter to you and if  not much  then ask yourself how important the  possibility  of a slightly slimmer display is to you  and finally  we should be expecting a pretty decent  battery life improvement  so if that by itself will make the  series 6 worth it for you  then you should definitely wait but if  you think the series 5 does everything  you currently need it to do  and you're not that excited for the new  features then i would consider  picking up a series 5 right now the only  downside is that there really aren't  many great sales going on  with the best price looking like four  hundred and nine dollars on amazon  about twenty dollars off for the 44  millimeter model  and i honestly don't think that the  price will go up much on the series six  maybe a maximum of fifty dollars or it  might even have the same price  so based on that if you can wait then  absolutely wait for the series 6.  if you enjoy this video go ahead and tap  the like button and click the circle  above to subscribe  and definitely be sure to check out our  apple product mask  down in the merch shelf below thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  [Music]  video

